# Trials/.gitignore
#
# Hides one-off debug-session scripts and generated output from `git add`,
# so they don't get swept into a commit by accident. This file only affects
# UNTRACKED items -- anything already committed (check_frac_*.py,
# stufe3_*.py, verify_jit_kernels.py, run_conservation.py, ...) is not
# touched by it; removing those from the repo is a separate, deliberate
# decision (`git rm`), not something a .gitignore can or should do silently.
#
# Nothing on disk is deleted by this file. To commit an ignored file anyway,
# `git add -f <path>`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output: data, logs, cache. Never source, always regenerable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Results/
debug_logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-off debug-session scripts.
#
# Each of these was written to investigate or patch ONE specific historical
# issue and says so in its own docstring. They are not general-purpose tests
# and are not meant to be re-run going forward -- keeping them out of commits
# avoids the repo silently accumulating one bugfix's throwaway tooling per
# session. If one of these turns out to still be useful, `git add -f` it and
# remove its line here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cleanup_and_run.py
rerun_bcd.py
validate_sensitivity_fix.py

# Regenerates test_droplet_10um_stable.py / test_droplet_20um_instable.py
# from test_powerlaw_rumpf_full.py (regex on DROPLET_DIAMETER) for one
# specific mass-conservation investigation (see Fundamentals.md). The
# generated copies below are stale the moment test_powerlaw_rumpf_full.py
# changes (they do not carry the SIZEEVAL/dW fixes from B-03/B-06); rerun
# this generator instead of hand-editing or committing its output.
test_runner_mass_debug.py
test_droplet_10um_stable.py
test_droplet_20um_instable.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audit probe scripts (2026-08-17/18 nucleation/mass-conservation review).
#
# Kept on disk -- they reproduce every measured number in
# docs/Audit_2026-08-17.md and docs/Audit_Umsetzung.md, so they're worth
# having locally to rerun a check. Not committed: the supervisor only needs
# code and documentation, not the throwaway verification harness that
# produced the numbers in that documentation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
audit/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working studies (decision of 2026-08-20).
#
# These are documented, general-purpose verification scripts rather than
# session debris -- an earlier version of this file argued for committing them
# on exactly that ground. They stay out of the repository anyway, because the
# supervisor needs the solver and its documentation, not the study scripts
# built on top of it. They remain on disk and keep working.
#
# To include one after all: delete its line here and `git add -f <path>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
test_agg_p1_sweep_highliquid.py
test_all_kernels.py
test_breakage_rate_coleval_parity.py
test_dry_mixer_kernels.py
test_initial_liquid_behavior.py
test_kint_more_liquid.py
test_sensitivity.py
test_sensitivity_repeats.py

# Everything else in this directory -- test_powerlaw_rumpf_full.py and the
# other committed scripts -- stays tracked and is not affected by this file.
# .gitignore only ever hides UNTRACKED items.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
